The registry's per-plugin lintSuppressions list is a human-maintained line-numbered mirror of each .eta template's front-config lintSuppressions block, which is what the compiler actually reads to suppress lint at build time; registry-reconciliation.test.ts checks only the aggregate count against lintSuppressionBudget, so a line-number or rule-name edit in one place that isn't mirrored in the other passes every test while becoming false documentation.
